# Optional resource limits for the Orca server container (Linux --role server), written into its compose.yaml.
# Nothing is set by default. Set values in manifest/local/server-limits.env (git-ignored), one KEY=VALUE per line;
# a key there replaces the same key here. Only these keys are accepted (Docker Compose service options):
#   mem_limit=<size>       memory for the whole container, e.g. 16g (sizes take b, k, m or g)
#   memswap_limit=<size>   memory plus swap; the same value as mem_limit means no swap
#   pids_limit=<n>         64 or more: processes and threads in the container
#   cpus=<n>               CPUs, e.g. 4 or 2.5
# They replace the native server's per-terminal ORCA_TERMINAL_* limits, which need systemd and do not apply inside a
# container. --apply re-creates the container when they change.
